WEBVTT

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.626
Excuse me, can you tell me
where I can find the supervisor?

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.686
Over there.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.323
Thank you.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.638
Your authorization
and licenses, please?

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:24.950
Level 6 in Thermodynamics
and Quantum Fusion.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.282
Well. Janeway.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.479
I'm impressed.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.715
Thank you, sir.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.280
Now, if you could just manage
to report to your shift on time.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.087
I'm sorry.
I boarded the wrong transport.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.286
I ended up

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.090
at the Atmosphere
Filtration Facility.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.154
They're always looking
for skilled workers.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.097
I'm surprised they didn't
offer you a job.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.634
I promise,
I won't be late again.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.169
Well, it's easy
to get disoriented

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.295
when you're new here.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.770
I've been in this city
all my life,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.239
and I still get lost
on occasion.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:51.471
Now, you'll be monitoring
the primary reactor coils.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.409
They process more
than 8,000 metric...

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.778
8,000 metric tons
of tylium per second

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.784
at 94 percent thermal
efficiency.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.547
I memorized the specifications.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.145
Let me know
if there's anything you need.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.215
You'll find we like
to keep our workforce happy.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.486
I can already tell

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.028
it's going to be much better
than my last job.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.583
The specifications
you asked for.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.025
Thanks.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:43.945
Input Error 415.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.315
Command Code Violation 2308.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.956
Come on,
shut off that damn alarm,

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:55.051
and I promise
I'll never violate you again.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.957
You almost started
a core overload.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.124
I would have corrected it.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.292
Well, I'm sorry
for interrupting then.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.596
And for eavesdropping.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.036
I overheard you talking
to your console.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.265
It's an old habit.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.500
Does it work?

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.838
I'm not sure this control panel
and I

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.571
speak the same language yet.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.806
Well, if you need
an interpreter...

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.314
Jaffen.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.475
Kathryn.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.813
I work just down there.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:20.910
That's good to know.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.784
This station doesn't
require two operators.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.915
I don't think we've met.
I'm...

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:28.118
Employee 1326.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:30.685
And you're Employee 8584.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.788
Since you're new here,
you may not be fully familiar

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.799
with the labor protocols,
but you should be aware

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.926
that fraternizing is not
permitted during work hours.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.266
And do you have a number
or maybe a name?

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.499
Annika Hansen.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:43.167
And what exactly is
your position here?

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.834
I'm the new Efficiency Monitor.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.812
Oh, I, uh, didn't
know they'd hired one.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.246
Now that you do, I suggest
you return to your station.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.647
We weren't fraternizing.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:53.948
He was just helping me
correct an input error.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.214
We're almost finished.

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.347
Do it quickly.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.447
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.253
I thought we were fraternizing.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.099
Maybe we could get
acquainted after work.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.692
Uh, there is a little place
some of us like to go to.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.702
We could get a meal.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:12.829
I can't.

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.897
You need to talk to someone
besides your console.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.773
I appreciate the offer,
but with this new job,

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:21.177
I don't really have time
to socialize.

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.852
They're always looking
for laborers

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.828
at the Power Distribution Plant.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.296
I had a job there once.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.559
Didn't like it much.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.601
Odd.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.398
They treat their employees well.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:46.938
How long were you there?

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:49.064
Oh, a while.

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:52.407
It would be very simple
for me to find out.

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:53.536
A day.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.877
A day?!

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.540
Half a day, actually.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.244
Give or take an hour.

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.752
Not what I'd call
an illustrious career.

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:05.621
I don't belong behind a console
pushing buttons.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.524
But when I heard
some of the workers

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:13.190
talking about your place,
I knew I had to get a job here.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.894
You were terminated,
weren't you?

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.526
Yes.

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:19.662
Oh... that's quite
an accomplishment

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:21.138
during a labor shortage.

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.139
What happened?

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:24.733
Oh... it's a long story.

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:28.042
I like a long story.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:31.174
I had a disagreement with
the new Efficiency Monitor.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.309
She didn't think
my work was very...

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.318
Efficient?

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:35.319
Exactly.

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:37.322
Then why should I hire you?

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:42.327
Well... there's my natural charm
and personality.

00:07:42.395 --> 00:07:44.659
They'd be a real asset
around a place like this,

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.595
where you're trying
to attract patrons.

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:48.065
I mean, look at you.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.261
You haven't been able
to tear yourself away from me.

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:52.736
There's no one else here.

00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.441
Please.

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:02.481
I really need the work.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.449
You'd better clean
those tables over there.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:09.420
This place is going to be
filled with hungry workers

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:11.218
as soon as the next shift ends.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.155
You won't regret this.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:16.195
Oh, I'm certain I will.

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:29.338
...all of them about my father,

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:31.603
and he couldn't understand
why I wasn't insulted.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:34.043
Finally, I just had to tell him:
I'm Norvalian.

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:35.740
I don't have a father.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.247
It wasn't that funny, Tuvok.

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:44.783
On the contrary.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:48.953
The man was ignorant
of how your species procreates.

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:53.791
His attempt to disparage you
ultimately humiliated him.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.635
Irony is often
a source of humor.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.570
Yes, well, when you explain it
like that, uh...

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.971
it's not funny at all.

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:05.169
I also have some
humorous anecdotes to share.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.872
I'll look forward
to hearing them.

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:10.380
I thought you didn't
have time to socialize.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.575
I'm not socializing.

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:14.677
I'm reviewing these manuals
and having something to eat.

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:16.551
Well, I recommend
the Latara broth,

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.112
and the section
on thermal coefficients.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.714
I'll join you.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:20.759
Really, I'm very, very busy.

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:21.850
Well, not to socialize.

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:24.829
To, uh, help you
review the manuals.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:28.632
How was your first day?

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:30.760
Here you are.

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:32.770
Compliments of the proprietress.

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:35.204
Tom.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.935
Uh, I'll be right back.

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.836
The proprietress
doesn't give away drinks.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.381
Well, I'm just
creating customer loyalty.

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:47.078
You've been creating loyalty
all night with those two women.

00:09:47.153 --> 00:09:49.644
I suggest you attend
to the other tables.

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:50.689
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.516
Here you are.

00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.562
Thank you.
Looks great.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:14.512
I can't believe
I let you keep me out this late.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.138
Well, I thought it
was my responsibility

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:17.807
to help you study those manuals.

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:19.214
Of course.

00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:20.377
And now that I have,

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:22.421
you should be less likely
to overload the core.

00:10:26.692 --> 00:10:28.751
You know, with all this
fascinating discussion

00:10:28.828 --> 00:10:29.954
about thermal coefficients,

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.723
you never told me
where you're from.

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:33.628
A planet called Earth.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.223
Never heard of it.

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:37.064
Oh, a long way from here.

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:38.398
What's it like?

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:41.963
Overpopulated, polluted,
very little work.

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:43.939
It sounds like my homeworld.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.342
Guess we're both
lucky to be here.

00:10:46.412 --> 00:10:47.640
It's nice to be in a place

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:49.738
where different species
get along so well.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:51.646
Oh, so, you admit
we're getting along.

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:54.618
I was speaking
in a broader cultural context.

00:10:54.687 --> 00:10:56.086
I see.

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:58.646
There's a lot of violence
where I come from.

00:10:58.724 --> 00:11:01.249
That's too bad.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:02.385
It's getting late.

00:11:02.461 --> 00:11:04.326
I still haven't adjusted
to the weather here.

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:05.455
It gets so cold at night.

00:11:05.531 --> 00:11:07.021
It's almost curfew.

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:09.795
Yes, sir.
We both live right here.

00:11:11.904 --> 00:11:13.394
Good night, then.

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:19.106
You know, one of the advantages
of living in employee housing

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:21.169
is that we can
continue sharing ideas

00:11:21.247 --> 00:11:22.942
even after the workday is over.

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:23.947
Is that so.

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:25.540
Yes, and I do have
a spectacular view

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:27.176
of the river
from my living quarters.

00:11:27.253 --> 00:11:29.483
I really have to get to sleep.

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:30.749
Maybe another time.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:33.519
I'm sorry if I'm making
you uncomfortable.

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:35.958
You're not.

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:37.962
Well, if you get lonely...

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:39.656
I'll let you know.

00:11:56.949 --> 00:11:58.211
It wasn't me.

00:11:59.652 --> 00:12:01.779
It's not an overload.
It's time for our inoculations.

00:12:01.854 --> 00:12:03.879
What inoculations?

00:12:03.956 --> 00:12:05.617
They're nothing to worry about.

00:12:05.691 --> 00:12:07.818
Protection against
ambient radiation.

00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:10.020
I didn't realize
that was a problem.

00:12:10.096 --> 00:12:12.530
It's not, as long as you're
inoculated regularly.

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:18.060
We're lucky to have an employer
that concerned about our safety.

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:19.263
It wasn't that bad.

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:20.430
It doesn't bother me.

00:12:20.506 --> 00:12:22.064
How long did it take to go away?

00:12:24.477 --> 00:12:26.069
Ten days, two weeks.

00:12:33.052 --> 00:12:34.110
Is something wrong?

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:36.381
Forgive me, but...

00:12:36.455 --> 00:12:38.616
I'm, I'm afraid of injections.

00:12:38.691 --> 00:12:40.784
I assure you, this is painless.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:45.422
Is-ls there some other method
of administering the medication?

00:12:45.498 --> 00:12:47.898
No, I'm afraid there isn't.

00:12:47.967 --> 00:12:49.264
Very well.

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.432
No!

00:12:55.508 --> 00:12:57.942
No! No!

00:12:58.444 --> 00:13:00.139
We're finished.

00:13:00.212 --> 00:13:01.873
You can go back to work.

00:13:03.983 --> 00:13:05.109
Next.

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:27.235
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 54584.3.

00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:29.774
Ensign Kim, Mr. Neelix
and I are returning to Voyager

00:13:29.842 --> 00:13:33.141
after five days of trading
with the Nar Shaddan.

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:36.511
In six years, I've never been
on an away mission

00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:37.947
worse than this one.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:40.348
I don't know
how you can say that.

00:13:40.419 --> 00:13:43.149
The cargo hold is crammed
with valuable supplies.

00:13:43.222 --> 00:13:44.951
And my stomach is crammed

00:13:45.057 --> 00:13:47.685
with alien parasites
doing back flips.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.423
I guess you shouldn't have drunk
that Falah nectar.

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:53.055
You insisted I try it.

00:13:53.132 --> 00:13:56.863
Uh! The Nar Shaddan
consider it a delicacy.

00:13:56.936 --> 00:13:58.904
To refuse would've
insulted them.

00:13:58.971 --> 00:14:02.873
I didn't hear you insisting
that Commander Chakotay try it.

00:14:02.942 --> 00:14:05.376
Commander Chakotay's
a vegetarian.

00:14:05.444 --> 00:14:08.106
It was made from meat?

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.909
More like a meat byproduct.

00:14:11.217 --> 00:14:12.684
I'm going to be sick.

00:14:12.751 --> 00:14:14.480
Not after you drink this.

00:14:14.553 --> 00:14:15.611
What is it?

00:14:15.688 --> 00:14:17.622
Leola bark tea.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.523
To settle even the
queasiest of stomachs.

00:14:20.593 --> 00:14:23.562
Ugh! It smells worse
than the meat nectar.

00:14:23.629 --> 00:14:27.190
I'll wait for the Doctor
to treat me.

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.166
At least I'll be sleeping
in my own bed tonight.

00:14:29.235 --> 00:14:31.760
Harry, I know you're not
feeling well, but I need you

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:33.737
and Neelix up here.

00:14:33.806 --> 00:14:34.932
On our way.

00:14:38.277 --> 00:14:40.507
Anything wrong, Commander?

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:41.511
We're at the rendezvous
coordinates,

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.480
but there's no sign of Voyager,

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:45.779
and they're not responding
to hails.

00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:47.944
Start scanning
on all frequencies.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:50.420
They've got to be
out there somewhere.

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:52.684
So much for my own bed.

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:02.499
Reinitialize
the subspace transponder.

00:15:02.568 --> 00:15:05.560
Warning.
Main computer is failing.

00:15:06.639 --> 00:15:09.403
Switch to backup processors.

00:15:09.475 --> 00:15:12.603
Main computer stabilized.

00:15:12.678 --> 00:15:15.238
Good. Now...
let's try this again.

00:15:15.314 --> 00:15:18.374
Reinitialize
the subspace transponder.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.781
Unable to comply.

00:15:19.852 --> 00:15:20.910
Why not?

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:22.247
Insufficient power.

00:15:22.321 --> 00:15:24.084
And they say I'm difficult.

00:15:24.156 --> 00:15:26.784
Reroute power
from the replicator system.

00:15:26.859 --> 00:15:27.917
Unable to comply.

00:15:28.027 --> 00:15:29.119
Clarify!

00:15:29.194 --> 00:15:31.594
Relays to the transponder
are fused.

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:32.722
Any suggestions?

00:15:32.798 --> 00:15:34.390
Please restate inquiry.

00:15:36.135 --> 00:15:39.536
Can the power relays
be bypassed?

00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:41.129
Negative.

00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:43.731
Then I suppose I'll have
to replace them by hand.

00:15:44.877 --> 00:15:46.071
Warning. Intruder alert.

00:15:46.145 --> 00:15:47.203
Where?

00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:48.473
The Bridge.

00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:49.605
How many?

00:15:49.682 --> 00:15:50.876
Two humanoids.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.076
Can you identify them?

00:15:52.151 --> 00:15:53.118
Negative.

00:15:53.185 --> 00:15:56.052
Sensor resolution
is below 20 percent.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.569
Stop what you're doing
and turn around!

00:16:18.344 --> 00:16:20.710
Take it easy, Doc!
It's us!

00:16:23.549 --> 00:16:25.574
It's good to see
some friendly faces.

00:16:25.651 --> 00:16:28.484
For that matter, it's good
to see any faces at all.

00:16:28.554 --> 00:16:31.114
I'm sorry I haven't gotten
life support back on line yet,

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.680
but since I've been
the only one aboard,

00:16:32.758 --> 00:16:33.747
it hasn't been a priority.

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:35.589
What the hell happened?

00:16:35.661 --> 00:16:37.424
We ran into some... problems.

00:16:37.496 --> 00:16:38.554
I can see that.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.097
Can you be
a little more specific?

00:16:40.165 --> 00:16:41.792
Of course.

00:16:43.535 --> 00:16:47.596
About... 12 hours after
you left on your away mission,

00:16:47.673 --> 00:16:49.368
things started to go wrong.

00:16:49.441 --> 00:16:52.569
We hit some sort
of subspace mine.

00:16:55.547 --> 00:16:58.880
Computer, transfer the EMH
to the mobile emitter.

00:16:58.951 --> 00:17:00.145
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:17:00.219 --> 00:17:01.777
Sick Bay to Engineering.

00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:03.321
Please respond.

00:17:03.389 --> 00:17:06.017
It wasn't long before
I was inundated with casualties,

00:17:06.091 --> 00:17:08.889
all suffering from
tetryon radiation poisoning.

00:17:08.961 --> 00:17:10.895
Pretty soon,
the Captain arrived.

00:17:10.996 --> 00:17:13.123
Doctor, can you
treat these people?

00:17:13.198 --> 00:17:14.426
I can stabilize them,

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.900
but if we can't contain
the radiation...

00:17:17.002 --> 00:17:19.527
Get everyone to the escape pods,
quickly.

00:17:19.605 --> 00:17:20.572
Not you, Doctor.

00:17:20.639 --> 00:17:21.628
I need you here.

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:22.901
Captain?

00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:24.067
Computer,

00:17:24.143 --> 00:17:26.134
activate the Emergency
Command Hologram.

00:17:26.211 --> 00:17:27.610
Authorization:

00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:29.476
Janeway-omega-3.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:33.381
Command codes transferred.

00:17:33.452 --> 00:17:35.920
You've wanted this chance
for a long time.

00:17:35.988 --> 00:17:37.046
Now you've got it.

00:17:37.122 --> 00:17:38.054
Aye, Captain.

00:17:38.123 --> 00:17:39.215
Try to vent the radiation.

00:17:39.291 --> 00:17:41.486
The rest of us will get out
of the contaminated area

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.357
and head for the nearest
habitable planet.

00:17:43.429 --> 00:17:44.453
You need medical care.

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.896
Unless someone answers
our distress call,

00:17:46.965 --> 00:17:47.932
we'll have to make due
with medkits.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.228
We'll rendezvous
as soon as it's safe

00:17:49.301 --> 00:17:50.598
to come back on board.

00:17:52.871 --> 00:17:55.135
Take good care of Voyager.

00:17:55.207 --> 00:17:57.334
You can count on me, Captain.

00:18:01.914 --> 00:18:04.280
The crew abandoned ship,

00:18:04.349 --> 00:18:07.216
and I began to assess
the damage caused by the mine.

00:18:07.286 --> 00:18:10.847
But before I could even get
started with the repairs,

00:18:10.923 --> 00:18:12.982
I got some unexpected company.

00:18:13.058 --> 00:18:14.616
Computer, report.

00:18:14.693 --> 00:18:16.320
An alien vessel has locked
onto Voyager

00:18:16.395 --> 00:18:18.056
with a tractor beam.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:19.392
Open a channel.

00:18:19.465 --> 00:18:21.797
This is the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:18:21.867 --> 00:18:23.494
Disengage your tractor beam.

00:18:23.569 --> 00:18:26.902
Our scans show no life signs
aboard your vessel.

00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:28.336
Identify yourself.

00:18:28.407 --> 00:18:30.375
I'm the Emergency
Command Hologram.

00:18:30.442 --> 00:18:31.466
"Hologram."

00:18:31.543 --> 00:18:32.532
That's right.

00:18:32.611 --> 00:18:34.272
Now release my ship.

00:18:34.346 --> 00:18:35.643
Your crew has abandoned it.

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:36.840
It belongs to me now.

00:18:36.915 --> 00:18:38.542
I beg to differ.

00:18:38.617 --> 00:18:44.112
Computer, target the vessel's
tractor emitter and fire.

00:18:47.326 --> 00:18:52.423
Come about, heading 903 mark 6.

00:18:52.498 --> 00:18:54.728
Engage at warp 2.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.064
Warp engines are off-line.

00:18:57.136 --> 00:18:58.831
Evasive pattern Beta-4.

00:18:58.904 --> 00:19:00.769
Target the vessel's engines.

00:19:07.779 --> 00:19:12.113
Warning. Two vessels
approaching, bearing 336 mark 1.

00:19:12.184 --> 00:19:14.152
Reverse course, full impulse.

00:19:14.219 --> 00:19:16.653
I managed to evade
the other two ships

00:19:16.722 --> 00:19:18.383
and hid inside this nebula.

00:19:18.457 --> 00:19:19.856
I vented the radiation,

00:19:19.925 --> 00:19:22.189
repaired as many systems
as I could,

00:19:22.261 --> 00:19:25.719
but with no help, let's just say
I'm glad you found me.

00:19:25.797 --> 00:19:28.664
It wasn't easy picking up
your homing signal.

00:19:28.734 --> 00:19:30.065
Well, I had to encrypt it.

00:19:30.135 --> 00:19:31.295
Every time I left the nebula,

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.600
I detected more ships
searching for me.

00:19:33.672 --> 00:19:34.900
Any idea who they are?

00:19:35.007 --> 00:19:39.239
No. But I've analyzed
all of their weapons signatures.

00:19:40.379 --> 00:19:42.904
They match the subspace mine.

00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:46.712
It was a deliberate attempt
to disable Voyager.

00:19:46.785 --> 00:19:49.253
Good thing you were here.

00:19:49.321 --> 00:19:52.552
What about the rest of the crew?

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:54.649
Not a word.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.471
Make them comfortable.

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.430
We're going to treat
your injuries.

00:20:34.499 --> 00:20:35.966
Who are you?

00:20:36.101 --> 00:20:37.591
My name is Dr. Kadan.

00:20:37.669 --> 00:20:40.797
You're in a Quarren
medical facility.

00:20:40.872 --> 00:20:42.362
My crew?

00:20:42.441 --> 00:20:43.635
My understanding is that

00:20:43.709 --> 00:20:46.303
they've all been rescued
from their escape pods.

00:20:46.378 --> 00:20:48.073
Treat my people first.

00:20:48.146 --> 00:20:50.114
Everyone will be taken care of.

00:20:53.652 --> 00:20:55.620
Thank you.

00:21:03.895 --> 00:21:05.726
What is that medication?

00:21:05.797 --> 00:21:08.789
An antiradiation serum,
perfectly safe.

00:21:17.442 --> 00:21:18.841
What are you doing?

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.276
She's suffering
from Dysphoria Syndrome.

00:21:21.346 --> 00:21:22.404
Don't worry, it's treatable.

00:21:28.887 --> 00:21:30.081
Release her immediately.

00:21:30.155 --> 00:21:31.850
Restrain him.

00:21:33.058 --> 00:21:34.025
Captain!

00:21:35.294 --> 00:21:38.286
No! No!

00:21:49.174 --> 00:21:50.106
Excuse me.

00:21:50.175 --> 00:21:51.836
Hi.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.502
I believe we know each other.

00:21:53.578 --> 00:21:54.510
You're Tuvok, right?

00:21:54.579 --> 00:21:56.376
We met last week
at the shift briefing.

00:21:56.448 --> 00:21:57.972
Before that.

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.745
Before we were working here.

00:21:59.818 --> 00:22:00.876
Oh, I don't think so.

00:22:00.952 --> 00:22:02.943
I mean, we're obviously not
from the same place.

00:22:04.189 --> 00:22:07.818
Still... I believe I know you.

00:22:07.893 --> 00:22:09.383
From the hospital perhaps?

00:22:09.461 --> 00:22:10.860
What hospital?

00:22:10.929 --> 00:22:13.090
...I am not certain.

00:22:13.165 --> 00:22:15.133
We... We were patients.

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:17.065
You must have me confused
with someone else.

00:22:17.135 --> 00:22:19.262
I've never been sick enough
to go to a hospital.

00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:21.329
I'm sorry, I have a lot
of work to finish.

00:22:21.406 --> 00:22:23.465
Please... try to remember.

00:22:23.542 --> 00:22:26.238
It-lt may be important.

00:22:26.311 --> 00:22:27.608
Is there a problem here?

00:22:27.679 --> 00:22:29.840
I think it's just
a misunderstanding.

00:22:29.915 --> 00:22:30.882
Tuvok?

00:22:33.885 --> 00:22:35.352
She's right.

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:36.512
It's, uh... it's a...

00:22:36.588 --> 00:22:37.816
It's a misunderstanding.

00:22:37.889 --> 00:22:38.856
You don't look well.

00:22:38.924 --> 00:22:40.915
Maybe you should go
to the infirmary.

00:22:40.992 --> 00:22:43.187
No, no, I'm fine. Fine.

00:22:43.261 --> 00:22:46.162
Uh... I'll go back
to my station.

00:22:46.231 --> 00:22:47.960
Sorry to have bothered you.

00:22:49.901 --> 00:22:50.959
What was that all about?

00:22:51.036 --> 00:22:53.095
I'm not sure.

00:22:53.171 --> 00:22:54.832
Strange man.

00:22:54.906 --> 00:22:57.704
And a terrible joke teller.

00:22:57.776 --> 00:22:59.641
So, are we having
dinner tonight?

00:22:59.711 --> 00:23:00.643
Again?

00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:02.009
What, you don't like my cooking?

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:03.672
No, it's wonderful.

00:23:03.749 --> 00:23:04.681
It's just...

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:05.682
I'm a perfectionist.

00:23:05.751 --> 00:23:06.740
I'm going to keep trying

00:23:06.818 --> 00:23:08.843
until I make you
the perfect meal.

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:11.514
And then we stop
eating together?

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:16.254
I'll have dinner with you.
On one condition:

00:23:16.328 --> 00:23:19.695
I make it.

00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:21.562
I think I can accept
those terms.

00:23:21.633 --> 00:23:22.827
Good.

00:23:22.901 --> 00:23:25.301
Now go back to your station
before the Efficiency Monitor

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.861
catches us fraternizing.

00:23:36.615 --> 00:23:38.640
Can I bring you something else?

00:23:38.717 --> 00:23:40.810
No, thank you.

00:23:40.886 --> 00:23:43.320
I haven't seen you
in here before.

00:23:43.388 --> 00:23:45.288
You probably just didn't notice.

00:23:45.357 --> 00:23:47.484
Oh, I'd have noticed.

00:23:49.694 --> 00:23:51.889
Well, apparently,
you aren't as observant

00:23:51.963 --> 00:23:53.453
as you think you are.

00:23:53.532 --> 00:23:54.521
Oh, really?

00:23:54.599 --> 00:23:56.590
I've been coming in here
the same time every day

00:23:56.668 --> 00:23:57.692
for the past two weeks.

00:23:57.769 --> 00:23:59.634
Well, that explains it.

00:23:59.704 --> 00:24:01.262
I usually work nights.

00:24:01.339 --> 00:24:02.863
Me, too.

00:24:02.941 --> 00:24:05.774
At the Power Distribution
Facility.

00:24:05.844 --> 00:24:07.311
You see? I am observant.

00:24:07.379 --> 00:24:09.779
Tom...

00:24:09.848 --> 00:24:12.408
Hmm... I need you for a moment.

00:24:12.484 --> 00:24:13.610
I'll be right there.

00:24:17.088 --> 00:24:20.421
Listen, you should come back in
when you get a night off.

00:24:20.492 --> 00:24:22.323
It's a lot more fun
when there's a crowd.

00:24:22.394 --> 00:24:24.589
I don't really like crowds.

00:24:24.663 --> 00:24:26.324
Well, then, maybe we
could get together

00:24:26.398 --> 00:24:28.457
during the day sometime,
take a walk by the river.

00:24:28.533 --> 00:24:29.465
I don't think so.

00:24:29.534 --> 00:24:30.466
Why not?

00:24:30.535 --> 00:24:34.198
I am a very engaging
conversationalist.

00:24:35.707 --> 00:24:36.867
Oh.

00:24:36.942 --> 00:24:39.206
Yeah.

00:24:39.277 --> 00:24:41.142
Still want to get together?

00:24:41.213 --> 00:24:43.306
You're married.

00:24:43.381 --> 00:24:45.042
No.

00:24:45.116 --> 00:24:47.584
Oh.

00:24:47.652 --> 00:24:49.779
Enjoy your day.

00:24:58.096 --> 00:25:02.897
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 54597.9.

00:25:03.034 --> 00:25:04.899
After restoring primary systems,

00:25:04.970 --> 00:25:08.064
we've left the nebula
to try to find the crew.

00:25:08.139 --> 00:25:10.198
Though there's still
a lot of damage,

00:25:10.275 --> 00:25:11.606
we have been able
to reconfigure sensors

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:14.110
to detect subspace mines.

00:25:14.179 --> 00:25:16.704
Ensign Kim's been running
continuous scans,

00:25:16.781 --> 00:25:18.612
but there's still
no sign of our people.

00:25:18.683 --> 00:25:21.277
On the bright side, the ships
that were searching for us

00:25:21.353 --> 00:25:22.786
seem to have given up.

00:25:22.854 --> 00:25:24.651
With only four people on board,

00:25:24.723 --> 00:25:26.384
repairs are going slowly.

00:25:30.662 --> 00:25:32.823
Power to the secondary
propulsion systems

00:25:32.898 --> 00:25:34.866
has been restored.

00:25:34.933 --> 00:25:35.922
Kim to the Doctor.

00:25:36.067 --> 00:25:37.466
Report to Astrometrics.

00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:39.265
On my way.

00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:42.607
Any luck?

00:25:42.674 --> 00:25:45.666
I've scanned ships and planets
in 83 systems.

00:25:45.744 --> 00:25:49.145
No humans, no Vulcans,
no Bolians...

00:25:49.214 --> 00:25:51.273
Maybe we can increase
the range of the sensors

00:25:51.349 --> 00:25:53.180
by tying them
into the main deflector.

00:25:53.251 --> 00:25:54.218
I've already done that.

00:25:54.286 --> 00:25:55.218
Oh.

00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:56.811
Well, we can boost
resolution by...

00:25:56.888 --> 00:25:58.480
I appreciate your input, Doc,

00:25:58.557 --> 00:26:01.321
but I didn't call you down here
to help me scan.

00:26:01.393 --> 00:26:04.260
I'm still feeling kind of queasy
from that nectar.

00:26:04.329 --> 00:26:05.762
I treated you days ago.

00:26:05.830 --> 00:26:08.094
Whatever you did hasn't worked.

00:26:08.166 --> 00:26:10.259
Maybe all those
command subroutines

00:26:10.335 --> 00:26:12.667
are compromising
your medical abilities.

00:26:14.005 --> 00:26:15.097
Maybe all that sarcasm

00:26:15.173 --> 00:26:17.539
is compromising
your natural charm.

00:26:24.115 --> 00:26:27.107
I've repaired
the deuterium injectors,

00:26:27.185 --> 00:26:29.415
brought secondary
propulsion back on line,

00:26:29.487 --> 00:26:32.752
and soothed Ensign Kim's
upset tummy.

00:26:32.824 --> 00:26:34.018
Good work.

00:26:34.092 --> 00:26:35.491
Why don't you get started

00:26:35.560 --> 00:26:38.154
on the ruptured plasma
conduits on Deck 10?

00:26:38.229 --> 00:26:41.562
Can't you take care of those?

00:26:41.633 --> 00:26:42.930
I beg your pardon?

00:26:43.034 --> 00:26:45.366
"Emergency Command Hologram."

00:26:45.437 --> 00:26:47.337
Doesn't that suggest
my place is here

00:26:47.405 --> 00:26:49.771
in Voyager's command center?

00:26:49.841 --> 00:26:51.502
Look, Doc, I'm impressed
with the way

00:26:51.576 --> 00:26:53.771
you handled yourself
while we were gone.

00:26:53.845 --> 00:26:56.040
But right now,
we've got to prioritize.

00:26:56.114 --> 00:26:57.877
Kim to Chakotay.

00:26:57.949 --> 00:26:58.881
Go ahead.

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:00.349
I've found them, Commander.

00:27:00.418 --> 00:27:02.181
They're on an M-Class planet.

00:27:02.253 --> 00:27:04.847
At maximum warp, we can be there
in less than three days.

00:27:04.923 --> 00:27:07.016
Transfer the coordinates
to the helm.

00:27:07.092 --> 00:27:08.889
I'll be in Astrometrics.

00:27:10.195 --> 00:27:11.253
Doctor...

00:27:11.329 --> 00:27:13.194
the Command Center is yours.

00:27:29.481 --> 00:27:31.210
Mmm, smells good.

00:27:31.282 --> 00:27:33.512
It's only burnt on the outside.

00:27:33.585 --> 00:27:36.110
Your cooking console's
a little temperamental, huh?

00:27:36.187 --> 00:27:38.155
Did you try talking to it?

00:27:38.223 --> 00:27:41.249
Once I cut off the charred part,
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:27:41.326 --> 00:27:43.556
Hmm.

00:27:55.206 --> 00:27:56.730
It's good.

00:27:56.808 --> 00:27:57.968
Really?

00:28:01.179 --> 00:28:03.147
Let's go.

00:28:03.214 --> 00:28:04.875
Where?

00:28:04.983 --> 00:28:06.177
I promised you dinner.

00:28:06.251 --> 00:28:08.515
We'll just have to get it
somewhere else.

00:28:08.586 --> 00:28:10.611
Wait.

00:28:10.689 --> 00:28:12.782
I'm not really hungry.

00:28:12.857 --> 00:28:13.881
Are you?

00:28:13.958 --> 00:28:15.391
No.

00:28:15.460 --> 00:28:16.791
Let's stay here.

00:28:29.774 --> 00:28:34.074
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 54608.6.

00:28:34.145 --> 00:28:36.079
We've traced
the crew's life signs

00:28:36.147 --> 00:28:38.342
to a large city on a planet
called Quarra.

00:28:38.416 --> 00:28:40.475
Unfortunately,
the local officials

00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:43.146
aren't being very cooperative.

00:28:43.221 --> 00:28:46.088
I have personally interviewed
several of the individuals

00:28:46.157 --> 00:28:47.283
on your crew manifest.

00:28:47.358 --> 00:28:49.121
None of them know who you are,

00:28:49.194 --> 00:28:51.856
nor have they heard
of a Starship Voyager.

00:28:51.930 --> 00:28:53.921
I'd like to speak to them
myself.

00:28:54.065 --> 00:28:55.327
That's not possible.

00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:56.731
If you're telling the truth,

00:28:56.801 --> 00:28:59.395
you have nothing to lose
by letting us talk to them.

00:28:59.471 --> 00:29:01.962
Unlike other planets
in this system,

00:29:02.040 --> 00:29:06.409
we grant our guest workers
the full protection of our laws.

00:29:06.478 --> 00:29:08.503
What exactly are you
protecting them from?

00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:11.606
Unscrupulous individuals
attempting to acquire

00:29:11.683 --> 00:29:12.741
skilled laborers.

00:29:12.817 --> 00:29:14.375
We're not trying
to acquire laborers.

00:29:14.452 --> 00:29:15.885
We're trying
to find our friends.

00:29:15.954 --> 00:29:17.888
Most of your friends
have excellent positions

00:29:17.989 --> 00:29:20.856
in the Central Power Facility
in the capitol.

00:29:20.925 --> 00:29:23.018
Why would any of them
want to travel thousands

00:29:23.094 --> 00:29:25.688
of light-years to a planet
on the other side of the galaxy,

00:29:25.764 --> 00:29:28.699
when they have safe,
comfortable lives right here?

00:29:28.767 --> 00:29:30.462
Because it isn't their home.

00:29:30.535 --> 00:29:34.665
I suggest you look elsewhere
to increase your labor supply.

00:29:34.739 --> 00:29:37.537
And if you attempt
to disturb any of our citizens,

00:29:37.609 --> 00:29:39.804
we will respond with force.

00:29:41.613 --> 00:29:42.807
Any luck?

00:29:42.881 --> 00:29:45.213
There's no way to beam them
through the shield grid.

00:29:45.283 --> 00:29:47.012
Take us out of orbit.

00:29:47.085 --> 00:29:48.848
We're not leaving them behind.

00:29:48.920 --> 00:29:50.046
No.

00:29:50.121 --> 00:29:52.146
But I want these people
to think we are.

00:30:09.207 --> 00:30:13.803
Hope the cooking console's
not being temperamental again.

00:30:13.878 --> 00:30:16.870
Making a hot drink
is one thing I can do.

00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:21.151
You're right.
It's good.

00:30:21.219 --> 00:30:22.584
I told you.

00:30:27.992 --> 00:30:30.790
Mmm.

00:30:30.862 --> 00:30:34.457
What's even better
is being here with you.

00:30:34.532 --> 00:30:36.727
Are you comfortable?

00:30:36.801 --> 00:30:39.929
The blanket's nice and warm.

00:30:40.004 --> 00:30:43.030
No, I mean here with me.

00:30:47.512 --> 00:30:51.881
I can't remember
being more comfortable...

00:30:51.950 --> 00:30:54.077
in my life.

00:30:56.421 --> 00:30:58.184
Yeah, I'll take care of it.

00:30:59.591 --> 00:31:01.786
Hi.

00:31:04.829 --> 00:31:06.922
Listen, I get off work
in a few minutes.

00:31:07.031 --> 00:31:08.498
I thought maybe you
and I could go to...

00:31:08.566 --> 00:31:10.397
You don't give up, do you?

00:31:10.468 --> 00:31:12.595
You don't even know
what I was gonna say.

00:31:12.670 --> 00:31:14.137
Let me guess.

00:31:14.205 --> 00:31:17.504
You're going to invite me
to take a walk by the river

00:31:17.575 --> 00:31:20.772
or maybe to your living quarters
to admire the view.

00:31:20.845 --> 00:31:22.938
Actually...

00:31:23.014 --> 00:31:24.948
I was going to offer
to introduce you

00:31:25.083 --> 00:31:26.243
to some people I met.

00:31:26.317 --> 00:31:29.445
A couple expecting
their first baby in a few weeks.

00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:34.617
I thought you might want to
get to know some other parents.

00:31:34.692 --> 00:31:36.159
You know, swap stories,

00:31:36.227 --> 00:31:39.025
maybe even find a playmate
for your baby.

00:31:41.065 --> 00:31:42.191
If it's a bad idea...

00:31:42.267 --> 00:31:44.258
No.

00:31:44.335 --> 00:31:46.166
No, it's nice.

00:31:46.237 --> 00:31:49.570
Listen, I'm sorry
about the other day.

00:31:49.641 --> 00:31:51.268
I'm the one
who should be apologizing.

00:31:51.342 --> 00:31:52.536
I shouldn't have assumed...

00:31:52.610 --> 00:31:53.872
- Forget it.
- Look, it's

00:31:53.945 --> 00:31:55.503
rare that I admit I'm wrong,

00:31:55.580 --> 00:31:58.913
so you might as well take
advantage of it while you can.

00:32:00.685 --> 00:32:03.916
It's been hard...

00:32:03.988 --> 00:32:06.786
being alone with a baby coming.

00:32:06.858 --> 00:32:08.792
I have a habit
of keeping my guard up.

00:32:08.860 --> 00:32:10.794
Well, that's understandable.

00:32:10.862 --> 00:32:13.763
It's just...
a romantic relationship

00:32:13.831 --> 00:32:15.822
is really out of the question
for me right now, and when

00:32:15.900 --> 00:32:17.367
- you started asking...
- How about a friend?

00:32:17.435 --> 00:32:18.800
What?

00:32:18.870 --> 00:32:22.601
Well, you said romance
is out of the question.

00:32:22.674 --> 00:32:25.006
Could you use a friend?

00:32:33.518 --> 00:32:34.849
Any progress?

00:32:34.919 --> 00:32:37.046
I've spoken to the
captains of eight vessels

00:32:37.121 --> 00:32:38.952
that left Quarra
in the last two weeks.

00:32:39.057 --> 00:32:40.820
No one knew anything
about the crew?

00:32:40.892 --> 00:32:41.950
No.

00:32:42.093 --> 00:32:44.152
But every one of them
asked me if I was looking

00:32:44.228 --> 00:32:45.286
for employment.

00:32:45.363 --> 00:32:47.456
Apparently, there's
a severe labor shortage

00:32:47.532 --> 00:32:48.590
throughout this system.

00:32:48.666 --> 00:32:50.657
There's a lot of competition
for workers.

00:32:50.735 --> 00:32:52.726
That ambassador said
most of our people

00:32:52.804 --> 00:32:54.863
were working
at the main power facility.

00:32:54.939 --> 00:32:57.567
I wonder if they still have
any positions to fill.

00:32:57.642 --> 00:33:00.372
I can make some inquiries.
Why?

00:33:02.113 --> 00:33:04.240
Because you and I are going
to find ourselves jobs.

00:33:04.315 --> 00:33:07.011
Reentering orbit
might arouse their suspicion.

00:33:07.085 --> 00:33:08.347
Not if we take my ship.

00:33:08.419 --> 00:33:09.477
Good idea, Neelix.

00:33:09.554 --> 00:33:11.454
Commander,
you've spoken directly

00:33:11.522 --> 00:33:13.490
with several
government officials.

00:33:13.558 --> 00:33:14.991
You could be recognized.

00:33:16.327 --> 00:33:20.229
Isn't reconstructive surgery
one of your specialties?

00:33:27.739 --> 00:33:31.641
I still say you should've
posed as a Talaxian.

00:33:31.709 --> 00:33:33.734
We'd have made a striking pair.

00:33:33.811 --> 00:33:35.438
Whiskers make me itch.

00:33:35.513 --> 00:33:36.537
How did it go?

00:33:36.614 --> 00:33:37.706
As soon as I

00:33:37.782 --> 00:33:39.579
told the supervisor
our qualifications,

00:33:39.650 --> 00:33:40.810
he was eager to hire us.

00:33:40.885 --> 00:33:43.353
He even helped me get
a docking permit for my ship.

00:33:43.421 --> 00:33:45.753
We'll be gainfully employed
by tomorrow morning.

00:33:45.823 --> 00:33:47.620
Here you go, Doc.

00:33:47.692 --> 00:33:49.159
Give me your hand, Mr. Neelix.

00:33:49.227 --> 00:33:50.159
What's this?

00:33:50.228 --> 00:33:51.490
A subdermal transponder.

00:33:51.562 --> 00:33:53.655
It will allow us
to maintain an open com-link

00:33:53.731 --> 00:33:55.926
so we can transport you
through the shield grid

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:57.558
if there's trouble.

00:33:57.635 --> 00:33:59.728
Hold position
at maximum transporter range.

00:33:59.804 --> 00:34:00.998
Aye, sir.

00:34:01.072 --> 00:34:03.336
I assumed I'd be in charge
during your absence, Commander.

00:34:03.408 --> 00:34:04.340
Excuse me?

00:34:04.409 --> 00:34:06.343
An Emergency Command Hologram,

00:34:06.411 --> 00:34:09.903
programmed with over two million
tactical subroutines,

00:34:09.981 --> 00:34:11.243
outranks an Ensign.

00:34:11.315 --> 00:34:12.873
A few words to the computer,

00:34:12.950 --> 00:34:15.646
and this Ensign
can delete those subroutines.

00:34:15.720 --> 00:34:18.018
Then you'd be depriving yourself

00:34:18.089 --> 00:34:20.387
of a skilled leader
for the sake of your ego.

00:34:20.458 --> 00:34:21.618
Oh, my ego!

00:34:21.692 --> 00:34:23.922
Gentlemen...

00:34:24.062 --> 00:34:25.154
work it out.

00:34:25.229 --> 00:34:28.130
Aye, sir.

00:34:50.755 --> 00:34:55.454
Employee 8583.

00:34:55.526 --> 00:34:57.494
Mr. Tuvok.

00:34:57.562 --> 00:34:59.655
According to my records,
you've neglected to report

00:34:59.730 --> 00:35:01.925
for your last three
inoculations.

00:35:03.968 --> 00:35:06.334
These inoculations are
for your protection.

00:35:08.406 --> 00:35:10.897
A sick worker is not
an efficient worker.

00:35:11.042 --> 00:35:14.637
Report to the infirmary.

00:35:14.712 --> 00:35:16.304
Seven of Nine.

00:35:16.380 --> 00:35:17.369
What?

00:35:17.448 --> 00:35:19.211
Seven of Nine.

00:35:19.283 --> 00:35:22.514
It's... your designation.

00:35:22.587 --> 00:35:25.055
My employee number is 8586.

00:35:25.123 --> 00:35:26.454
Take your hands off me!

00:35:26.524 --> 00:35:28.048
Call Security!

00:35:34.532 --> 00:35:37.092
I don't believe you are
who you think you are!

00:35:38.236 --> 00:35:39.567
We don't belong here.

00:35:39.637 --> 00:35:40.569
We don't belong here!

00:35:40.638 --> 00:35:44.335
This isn't right!

00:35:44.408 --> 00:35:46.774
We don't belong here!

00:35:55.386 --> 00:35:58.219
Qualification Level 3
in microkinetics.

00:35:58.289 --> 00:36:00.689
You could use
some improvement there.

00:36:00.758 --> 00:36:03.386
Level 5
in thermionic conversion.

00:36:03.461 --> 00:36:04.723
Good.

00:36:04.795 --> 00:36:07.491
We lost a thermionic
specialist yesterday.

00:36:07.565 --> 00:36:08.589
Did he find a better job?

00:36:08.666 --> 00:36:10.429
Uh, health problems.

00:36:10.501 --> 00:36:12.093
Someone you know?

00:36:12.170 --> 00:36:15.003
No, just... an unusual species.

00:36:15.072 --> 00:36:16.164
We have a diverse workforce.

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:19.676
Our thermionic converters
operate on a rotating frequency,

00:36:19.744 --> 00:36:21.905
so they have to be
closely monitored.

00:36:22.013 --> 00:36:25.676
You'll be required to report
your readings to the Controller

00:36:25.750 --> 00:36:27.012
at regular intervals.

00:36:27.084 --> 00:36:28.312
Any questions?

00:36:32.990 --> 00:36:35.356
Are you listening to me?

00:36:35.426 --> 00:36:36.916
Sorry, sir.

00:36:36.994 --> 00:36:38.962
I'm just excited to be here.

00:36:40.998 --> 00:36:42.966
Carry on.

00:36:57.148 --> 00:36:58.445
Kathryn.

00:36:58.516 --> 00:36:59.778
Yes.

00:36:59.850 --> 00:37:01.841
It's Chakotay.

00:37:01.919 --> 00:37:03.477
I'm sorry?

00:37:05.256 --> 00:37:06.723
I'm new here.

00:37:06.791 --> 00:37:08.759
The supervisor said you
would be a good person

00:37:08.826 --> 00:37:10.293
to speak to
if I had any questions.

00:37:10.361 --> 00:37:12.795
Mm. What can I help you with?

00:37:12.863 --> 00:37:14.626
Nothing.

00:37:14.699 --> 00:37:17.099
I just wanted
to introduce myself.

00:37:17.168 --> 00:37:19.659
Oh, what did you say
your name was?

00:37:19.737 --> 00:37:21.398
Chakotay.

00:37:21.472 --> 00:37:25.340
Actually, that's just
what my friends call me.

00:37:25.409 --> 00:37:27.900
My employment file
lists my given name:

00:37:27.979 --> 00:37:30.573
Amal Kotay.

00:37:30.648 --> 00:37:31.910
Well, whatever your name is,

00:37:32.016 --> 00:37:33.916
I'm happy to help you
any way I can.

00:37:37.655 --> 00:37:38.781
No, no!

00:37:38.856 --> 00:37:40.551
You're experiencing

00:37:40.625 --> 00:37:42.217
a relapse of Dysphoria Syndrome.

00:37:42.293 --> 00:37:44.158
This is going to make you
feel better.

00:37:44.228 --> 00:37:47.095
Get away from me!

00:37:48.466 --> 00:37:50.900
Losing my job there
was the best thing

00:37:50.968 --> 00:37:52.595
that ever happened to me.

00:37:52.670 --> 00:37:53.932
Why is that?

00:37:54.071 --> 00:37:56.164
Well, so many rules
and regulations.

00:37:56.240 --> 00:37:58.208
It was like
a military operation.

00:37:58.276 --> 00:37:59.504
I know what you mean.

00:37:59.577 --> 00:38:01.670
"Report here, reroute
power there."

00:38:01.746 --> 00:38:04.112
It's almost like serving
aboard a starship.

00:38:05.983 --> 00:38:07.109
Have you ever done that?

00:38:07.184 --> 00:38:10.017
You're looking
at the former captain

00:38:10.087 --> 00:38:12.021
of his own cargo vessel.

00:38:12.089 --> 00:38:14.683
Hmm, must be quite a life.

00:38:14.759 --> 00:38:15.885
What about you?

00:38:15.993 --> 00:38:17.790
Ever worked on a ship?

00:38:17.862 --> 00:38:18.988
Oh, no.

00:38:19.063 --> 00:38:20.587
Space travel makes me sick.

00:38:23.968 --> 00:38:25.128
I'm not lying.

00:38:25.202 --> 00:38:28.330
So, do you know most of the
people that come in here?

00:38:28.406 --> 00:38:30.636
A lot of them.

00:38:30.708 --> 00:38:33.040
This is a great place to work.

00:38:33.110 --> 00:38:34.338
Seems like it.

00:38:34.412 --> 00:38:36.573
I could put in a good word
for you to my employer.

00:38:36.647 --> 00:38:37.807
Ah, Neelix.

00:38:37.882 --> 00:38:40.009
I was wondering
when you'd get here.

00:38:40.084 --> 00:38:42.780
Amal Kotay, this is
my new friend, Tom Paris.

00:38:42.853 --> 00:38:43.911
What can I get you?

00:38:44.055 --> 00:38:45.545
That looks good.

00:38:47.658 --> 00:38:50.627
I was assigned
to the primary fusion chamber

00:38:50.695 --> 00:38:52.686
along with Mulcahey and Celes.

00:38:52.763 --> 00:38:54.594
Neither of them recognized me.

00:38:54.665 --> 00:38:55.689
Let me guess.

00:38:55.766 --> 00:38:57.427
They really love their jobs.

00:38:57.501 --> 00:39:00.959
It's like they've all been
programmed to be happy here.

00:39:01.038 --> 00:39:03.131
It's a safe bet
they're not going

00:39:03.207 --> 00:39:05.141
- to leave willingly.
- Here you go.

00:39:12.016 --> 00:39:13.677
Hi. How was your first day?

00:39:13.751 --> 00:39:14.979
Not bad.

00:39:15.052 --> 00:39:17.350
Would you and your friend
like to join us?

00:39:17.421 --> 00:39:19.582
That would be nice.

00:39:19.657 --> 00:39:22.751
Um, actually, I was hoping
we could eat alone tonight.

00:39:24.161 --> 00:39:26.356
Maybe another time.

00:39:29.533 --> 00:39:30.522
That was rude.

00:39:30.601 --> 00:39:32.034
I'm sorry.
I just, um...

00:39:32.103 --> 00:39:35.004
There's something I'd like
to talk to you about.

00:39:38.409 --> 00:39:39.341
Thanks.

00:39:39.410 --> 00:39:40.536
- Bye-bye.
- Thank you for joining us.

00:39:41.779 --> 00:39:44.145
B'Elanna.

00:39:44.215 --> 00:39:45.409
I'm due for a break.

00:39:45.483 --> 00:39:47.314
I'll walk you to the transport.

00:39:47.385 --> 00:39:49.046
Stop worrying.
I'll be fine.

00:39:49.120 --> 00:39:51.384
It's not you
that I'm worried about.

00:39:51.455 --> 00:39:55.084
The baby will be fine, too.

00:40:07.538 --> 00:40:10.098
So, what I was thinking is...

00:40:11.876 --> 00:40:15.903
...if we were to combine
our resources,

00:40:15.980 --> 00:40:18.471
we would reduce our expenses.

00:40:20.785 --> 00:40:24.243
Are you asking me to move in?

00:40:24.321 --> 00:40:26.289
Yes.

00:40:27.858 --> 00:40:29.723
I know it's impulsive.

00:40:29.794 --> 00:40:33.821
I... know we haven't known
each other very long, but...

00:40:33.898 --> 00:40:37.800
things are so easy
when we're together.

00:40:37.868 --> 00:40:39.426
And I just thought I...

00:40:39.503 --> 00:40:41.698
Okay.

00:40:41.772 --> 00:40:44.502
What?

00:40:44.575 --> 00:40:47.305
Maybe I'm out of my mind...

00:40:48.446 --> 00:40:50.778
...but let's try it.

00:40:53.584 --> 00:40:55.745
I think this is gonna be
a lot of fun, don't you?

00:40:55.820 --> 00:40:57.378
It's gonna be great.
You'll see.

00:40:57.455 --> 00:40:58.683
Yeah.

00:40:58.756 --> 00:40:59.882
Yeah, they're waiting for us.

00:40:59.957 --> 00:41:01.219
Come on, we got to go,
all right?

00:41:07.932 --> 00:41:09.194
Oh, excuse me.

00:41:09.266 --> 00:41:10.790
It was my fault.

00:41:10.868 --> 00:41:12.859
I should watch where I'm going.

00:41:12.937 --> 00:41:14.700
B'Elanna?

00:41:14.772 --> 00:41:16.933
How do you know my name?

00:41:17.041 --> 00:41:19.669
What if I told you
we were old friends?

00:41:21.812 --> 00:41:23.575
That's a ridiculous statement.

00:41:23.647 --> 00:41:26.844
I know it sounds strange,
but I can prove it to you.

00:41:26.917 --> 00:41:29.283
Look, I'm sorry,
but I'm late for work.

00:41:29.353 --> 00:41:30.342
Let go of me!

00:41:30.421 --> 00:41:31.979
I'm not going to hurt you.

00:41:34.625 --> 00:41:36.422
- Security, help.
- Chakotay to Voyager.

00:41:36.494 --> 00:41:38.086
We've got B'Elanna.

00:41:38.162 --> 00:41:40.687
Lock on to Neelix's signal,
and transport them to Sick Bay.

00:41:40.764 --> 00:41:41.924
Acknowledged.

00:41:41.999 --> 00:41:43.591
Help me!

00:41:43.667 --> 00:41:45.430
Let her go!

00:41:49.740 --> 00:41:51.332
Stop!

00:41:51.408 --> 00:41:53.706
Harry, I need
an emergency transport now!

00:41:54.979 --> 00:41:57.243
Sorry, Commander,
we're under attack.

00:41:57.314 --> 00:41:58.781
I had to raise shields.

00:42:04.388 --> 00:42:05.912
No, leave me alone!

00:42:06.023 --> 00:42:07.615
We're friends.
We're trying to help you.

00:42:07.691 --> 00:42:09.090
No, don't touch me!

00:42:40.457 --> 00:42:42.550
He turned into the accessway.

00:42:42.626 --> 00:42:44.685
I'll call for reinforcements.

00:42:58.976 --> 00:43:00.102
I think he went in there!

00:43:00.177 --> 00:43:01.735
Be careful!
He might be armed!
